.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Large reference PDFs/scans (exceed GitHub 100MB limit) - keep local only.
chicago/reference/Andreas-History_of_Chicago.pdf
chicago/reference/planning/Andreas-History_of_Chicago.pdf

# Large video captures - keep local only
chicago/reference/movies/

# Chicago reference corpus: large source files migrated to Internet Archive.
# Canonical copies live at archive.org/details/chicago1835-*; originals sit
# locally at projects/archive/data/chicago/reference/ (sibling to this repo,
# not tracked). See the *.yaml / SOURCE.yaml pointer files in chicago/reference/
# and CORPUS_MANIFEST.csv for the mapping. Guards below catch big originals
# being re-downloaded into the tracked dirs by mistake.
chicago/reference/fergus/*.pdf
chicago/reference/walkthroughs/*.mov
chicago/reference/newspapers/**/*.pdf
chicago/reference/newspapers/*.pdf
# The small newspaper transcriptions in newspapers/Transcriptions/ ARE committed.
chicago/reference/hh-porter-a-short-autobiography/*.pdf
chicago/reference/chicago-massacre-1812/*.pdf
chicago/reference/additional/vital-records-1871+/*.pdf

# IPUMS extracts: redistribution prohibited by IPUMS license (published to
# Internet Archive anyway, see ipums-usa.yaml/ipums-nhgis.yaml, but kept out
# of git regardless). Originals live at
# projects/archive/data/chicago/reference/ipums/.
# See chicago/reference/ipums/README.md.
chicago/reference/ipums/*.csv
chicago/reference/ipums/*.pdf
chicago/reference/ipums/nhgis0001_csv/
chicago/reference/ipums/nhgis0001_csv.zip
chicago/reference/ipums/nhgis0001_shape/
chicago/reference/ipums/nhgis0001_shape.zip
!chicago/reference/ipums/README.md

# CHICAGO 4D — THE BUILD PRODUCTS ARE GENERATED, SO THEY ARE NOT COMMITTED
# (T-0937 took the ticket board off the PR surface; T-0938 takes the rest of the
# published mirror off it, which is the whole of `site/4d/`).
#
# `tickets/BOARD.md` and `tickets/tickets.json` are pure functions of the one-file-
# per-ticket records in `chicago/4d/tickets/`, and everything under
# `site/4d/` is a pure function of `chicago/4d/` run through
# `chicago/4d/tools/publish.sh`. `tools/ticket.mjs` writes the first two, and every
# command that changes a ticket rewrites them — which means a run's FIRST commit
# (`ticket.mjs claim`) touches them before it has done any work at all. publish.sh
# writes the mirror, and its last act is to stamp the head sha and a wall clock into
# `build.json` and `walk/index.html`, so EVERY publishing branch rewrites those two
# by construction.
#
# That is what made them the most-conflicting files in the repository. Measured on PR
# #906 (the .gitattributes note beside this one): dev moved five times under one PR and
# every merge conflicted in generated files and never in the substantive diff; lap 5 was
# the ticket artifacts and nothing else. GitHub's server-side merge does not run this
# repo's merge drivers (T-0857), so `merge=generated` could not help the merge that
# decides mergeability, and each collision cost a hand lap.
#
# A file that is not tracked cannot conflict — in a clone or on the server. Nothing is
# lost by not committing any of it, because every one of these files has a command that
# writes it and a gate that refuses it stale:
#
#   tickets/BOARD.md, tickets/tickets.json   `ticket.mjs check` / `board`
#   site/4d/**                       `tools/publish.sh`, and `tools/check.sh`
#                                            now RUNS publish.sh and then asks
#                                            `check_published.mjs` whether what it
#                                            produced matches its source (T-0938).
#
# And every consumer builds it before it reads it: `publish.sh` regenerates the board
# before its copy, `deploy.yml` publishes the production tree AND the dev-preview
# worktree before the Pages upload, and `chicago-4d-bake.yml` publishes before it
# uploads the mirror the smoke runs against. So `/chicago/4d/`, `/chicago/4d/walk/`,
# `/chicago/4d/js/changelog.js` and `/chicago/4d/tickets.json` are all unchanged URLs.
#
# THE ONE FILE IN THIS SET THAT STAYS TRACKED is `chicago/4d/tools/dev-smoke-state.json`
# (T-0938, from T-0857 point 5): it sits in the same conflict set and looks like a build
# product, but it is an append-only register of smoke readings that nothing regenerates.
# Evidence is not regenerable. It keeps its merge driver instead — see /.gitattributes.
chicago/4d/tickets/BOARD.md
chicago/4d/tickets/tickets.json
site/4d/
